Package: cipher-platform
Version: 2.0
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Depends: dkms, libc6, libstdc++6, libgcc-s1, python3 (>= 3.10), python3-yaml, nvidia-container-toolkit (>= 1.17)
Recommends: linux-headers-generic, vllm
Conflicts: cipher-platform (<< 2.0)
Replaces: cipher-platform (<< 2.0)
Maintainer: CIPHER Platform <anil.0666369@gmail.com>
Description: CIPHER GPU efficiency platform - runtime, substrate, kmod, container injection
 V1 Phase B deployment artifact for neocloud GPU node operators. Bundles the
 CUDA injection runtime (libcipher_rt), the Phase 3 substrate (libcipher_v2),
 the pinned ABI-stable c10 core (libc10), the cipher_vllm plugin chain
 (KV-dedup + KV-offload + KV-bridge + model fingerprint) as a Python
 dist-info package, and the cipher_kmod kernel module shipped as DKMS source
 (rebuilds against running kernel). Postinst patches the host's CDI spec at
 /var/run/cdi/nvidia.yaml so that vanilla `docker run --gpus all` invocations
 transparently load the CIPHER substrate via nvidia-container-toolkit;
 end-user vLLM workloads are not modified. Operator-facing tooling:
 cipher-platform CLI (status/verify/refresh/version/logs), runbook, standalone
 health-check, systemd path-watcher for auto re-patch on driver upgrades.
